-- a rate that reads more than one constituent, which is what a pH-rate profile is. The observed rate of a
-- change in water is the sum of an uncatalysed term, an acid-catalysed term proportional to the hydronium
-- concentration and a base-catalysed term proportional to the hydroxide concentration -- the standard form
-- k0 + kH[H+] + kOH[OH-]. Read as orders of magnitude the sum is the larger of the terms, and adding the
-- amounts is the model this layer can carry: tag 3 is hydronium, tag 1 hydroxide.
brate-acid-base : Nat → Nat → Nat → Bath → Nat
brate-acid-base atag btag k0 v = plus k0 (plus (sol-amount atag (bath-sol v)) (sol-amount btag (bath-sol v)))
